course: dictionary
lesson: 1396
title: Caramel: a sweet that is also a change
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Caramel is a brown, sticky sweet, and it is also a colour. The word can be a noun (a sweet) or an adjective (a colour, like caramel-brown hair). The words around it show you which one you are reading.
explain: «Caramel is sugar broken down by strong heat into new substances; hot caramel is much hotter than boiling water and sticks to skin.» The clues are sugar, strong heat and hot. Caramel is what you get when sugar is heated until it melts and turns brown.
explain: Heating sugar is a change that cannot be reversed. White sugar melts and turns brown, and you cannot turn the caramel back into white sugar. Hot caramel sticks to skin, so only make it with an adult.
fact: Caramel is a sweet, brown, sticky food made by heating sugar until it melts and turns brown.
fact: A caramel is a chewy sweet made from sugar, butter and milk.
fact: Caramel is also a light brown colour, as in a caramel colour.
fact: «Hot caramel is much hotter than boiling water and sticks to skin.» Always ask an adult to help.
fact: Caramel is used in desserts, sauces, sweets and ice cream.
exercise: Caramel is made by doing what to sugar? | Shaking it in a jar | Mixing it with cold water | *Heating it until it melts and turns brown | Freezing it until it is hard
exercise: «Hot caramel is much hotter than boiling water and sticks to skin.» Why is this a safety rule? | It is cold and freezes your hands | It makes your hands smell sweet | It turns into water when you touch it | *It is very hot and sticks to skin, so an adult must help
exercise: In a shop, a child says the cushion is caramel. What is the most likely meaning? | A sweet to eat | *A light brown colour | A kind of cold drink | A tall building
test: In «a caramel colour», what kind of word is caramel? | Verb | Noun, meaning a sweet | *Adjective | Adverb
test: Heating sugar to make caramel is a permanent change. Why? | It turns cold again when you leave it | It just looks different in the light | It becomes water and disappears | *White sugar melts and turns brown, and it cannot be turned back
exam: The sentence «Caramel is sugar broken down by strong heat into new substances.» tells us what? | *Caramel is made when strong heat changes sugar into new substances | Sugar and caramel are always the same | Caramel is a kind of rice | Caramel is cold sugar in a bag
